# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MGFR — ignore rules
#
# The single most important rule in this file: character IP assets are NEVER
# committed. The 祀 model ReadMe forbids redistribution (二次配布), and the
# 小酒狐 voice weights and the LLM key are private too.
# See docs/asset-policy.md before editing this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Character IP: original model drop -------------------------------------
# The unpacked model folder sits at the repo root and must never be staged.
【明日方舟：终末地】祀_*/
# Belt and braces: block MMD source assets anywhere in the tree.
**/*.pmx
**/*.pmd
**/*.vmd
**/*.vpd

# --- Character IP: converted / derived assets ------------------------------
/converted/
/assets/Character/
**/*.fbx
**/*.blend
**/*.blend[0-9]

# Derived from 祀, so it stays out of the repo for the same reason the model
# does. Note that ``/assets/Character/`` above does NOT cover this: gitignore
# patterns are case-sensitive on Windows, so the lowercase, rooted rule never
# matched ``Assets/MGFR/...``. These two explicit rules do.
#
# The character scene is deliberately built so that losing these files does not
# break the project: nothing in the scene references them by GUID. The scene
# carries only the bootstrap component, and ``SiCharacterLoader`` builds the mesh
# from ``StreamingAssets/si`` at runtime. A fresh clone therefore opens the
# character scene and reports "character data missing - run MGFR > Copy
# Character Data" instead of failing to load. Regenerate with:
#   python -I tools/pmx/convert_si.py "<祀.pmx>" H:\MGFR\converted\si
#   Unity menu: MGFR > Copy Character Data
/unity-client/Assets/MGFR/Generated/
/unity-client/Assets/StreamingAssets/si/

# --- Scratch: probe renders, service logs, build output ---------------------
# batch/ holds working output rather than project content. The renders in it
# are pictures of 祀, so they carry the same redistribution restriction as the
# model, and they are PNGs - which nothing else in this file excludes. Without
# this rule a single `git add -A` would stage them.
/batch/

# --- Character IP: texture sets (both folders shipped with the model) ------
**/textures/
**/other tex/
# Generic texture blocks are deliberately narrow; add explicit paths if a
# legitimate, redistributable texture is ever needed in-tree.

# --- Voice: 小酒狐 weights and reference audio -----------------------------
**/*.ckpt
**/*.pth
**/*.onnx
**/*.wav
**/*.mp3
**/*.flac
**/*.m4a

# --- Downloaded engine models ----------------------------------------------
# Not IP-restricted, but large and fetched on demand (Silero VAD, SenseVoice).
/dialogue-service/models/

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
/dialogue-service/config.toml
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.key
**/secrets/
**/credentials*.json

